      "content": "I'm really sorry to hear that you're feeling this way, but it's important to be cautious. Taking extra electrolytes might temporarily alleviate mild dehydration, but it won't address the underlying issue like diabetes insipidus or diabetes. Using insulin without proper medical guidance, even from family, can be very dangerous and potentially life-threatening. It's crucial to seek professional medical help to safely and correctly manage your condition. Waiting a few more days over solutions that aren't guided by healthcare professionals isn't recommended. I encourage you to talk to a medical professional as soon as you can. They can provide the proper treatment and guidance to help you feel better safely and effectively.",
